{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Chirped-mirror",
  "Notes": "Dispersive mirror, 700-900 nm: Rs at least 99.5% from 700 to 900 nm, and a group delay dispersion of -50 fs^2 (s, normal incidence) from 750 to 850 nm.\n\nCaveats:\n- Manufacturability is scored with MINT/MAXT (minimum and maximum layer thickness) at a low weight. A sensitivity term (SENS) would score robustness to thickness errors directly, but it needs second derivatives of the merit function and is not offered; MINT/MAXT keep layers depositable and have exact derivatives.\n- The materials are constant-index, so their own dispersion adds nothing to GD or GDD. For numbers a real coating would show, replace them with the database TiO2 and SiO2 (Edit \u003E Materials).",
